{
 "sheet": "weapons",
 "note": "Megabonk weapons as skills for the Megabonk survivors only. Each survivor starts with its startWeapon (characters.json) on primary (left mouse); weapons picked on level up fill secondary (right mouse), utility (Shift) and special (R) in pick order: 4 weapons per run. Picking an owned weapon again levels it (+25% damage per level). kind: bullet | projectile | melee | aura | lightning. damage = x base damage per hit; interval = seconds between attacks (attack speed shortens it); cooldown = seconds between uses on slots 2-4; range = bullet range or melee/aura radius (m); prefab = RoR2 projectile address; effect = tracer (bullet) or swing/nova effect address; damageType none|ignite|bleed|slow|poison. mbIcon = exact Megabonk Texture2D name. mbSound = Megabonk AudioClip played on every attack instead of the RoR2 sound (empty: no short Megabonk sound fits, the RoR2 sound stays). mbProjectile = Megabonk model the projectile shows instead of its RoR2 look (projScale, projSpin deg/s); weapons without one have only particle effects in Megabonk, so they keep RoR2's. mb* = Megabonk's own WeaponData (sharedassets1, read with Il2CppDumper's layout): mbDamage per hit (x tuning weapon_damage_scale = damage coefficient; 0 = use damage), mbProjectiles shots per attack (0: a constant attack that ticks), fired one after another over mbBurstTime (at least mbMinBurstInterval apart), then mbEndCooldown before the next attack; attack speed divides all of it (Megabonk's WeaponUtility.GetWeaponCooldown). mbRange = targeting range (closest enemies first; 0 = melee/aura: range is used). mbOnlyClose: holds fire while no enemy is in range. mbCritChance adds to crit chance, mbProc is the proc coefficient. Weapons fire by themselves, as in Megabonk; interval and cooldown are no longer used. mbUpgrades = the weapon's Megabonk UpgradeData that this mod applies (damage = flat Megabonk damage, projectiles = more shots, size = radius/area x(1+v), crit = crit chance); each weapon level beyond the first applies the next one in order, cycling (Megabonk rolls a random few per level; the fixed order needs no network message). mbFx* = Megabonk's own effect prefabs for the weapon (MegabonkFx rebuilds their particle systems): mbFxMuzzle plays where a shot leaves, mbFxShot is the attack itself, placed by mbFxMode (fly: travels to the target at mbFxSpeed m/s; burst: at the muzzle towards the target; beam: a line to the target; slash: at the body towards the target; strike: at the target; ghost: on the Risk of Rain 2 projectile, replacing its look; aura: kept on the body, sized to the reach; stream: kept on the body, pointing at the target), mbFxHit plays where it lands; mbFxScale sizes them. Paths below a prefab name pick one child (PoisonFlaskProjectile/SmokeTrail).",
